<title>GERMANY: Veba, RWE, C&amp;W to merge German telcoms.</title>
<headline>Veba, RWE, C&amp;W to merge German telcoms.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's two largest utilities, RWE AG and Veba AG, and British-based Cable and Wireless will merge their German telecommunications actitivies, Veba said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Under the deal, the companies would set up a network services company, in which RWE will hold a majority of 51 percent, and a telecoms services company, in which the Vebacom venture of Veba and C&amp;W will hold the majority.</p>
</text>
